---
import { Code } from "@astrojs/starlight/components";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const quickStart = `mkdir -p ~/arrivo && cd ~/arrivo
curl -fsSLO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sdesmond/arrivo/main/docker-compose.yml
docker compose up -d`;
---

<section class="home-band not-content">
  <div class="home-band__copy">
    <p class="home-eyebrow">Self-hosting</p>
    <h2 class="home-h2">One compose file. Two containers.</h2>
    <p>
      Arrivo is the app plus PostgreSQL 17. Download one compose file, start it, and open the address. The app
      prepares its own database on every start.
    </p>
    <ul class="home-checks">
      <li>Runs on amd64 and ARM64: a Linux server, a NAS or a Raspberry Pi.</li>
      <li>No <code>.env</code> file and no secret to generate.</li>
      <li>The first visit creates the admin account. After that there is no public sign-up.</li>
      <li>Your trips and documents stay on your hardware. There is no hosted service to sign up for.</li>
      <li>Open source under AGPL-3.0.</li>
    </ul>
    <a class="home-link" href={`${base}/self-hosting/`}>Read the self-hosting guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </div>
  <div class="home-band__code">
    <Code code={quickStart} lang="bash" title="Terminal" frame="terminal" wrap />
    <p class="home-band__note">Then open <code>http://&lt;your-server&gt;:4850</code>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
